Herdr Enhanced: Files Enhanced and Git Enhanced, mods for the Herdr app, and a layout with them

This product includes software from Herdr (https://herdr.dev), licensed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE). From the Herdr app 0.1.14, modified:

- the Files mod that ships with it (mods/files): the base of
  files-enhanced/mods/files-enhanced/ (main.js, tree.js, place.js, preview.js, the
  listing in machine.js) and its icons chevron-down.svg, chevron-right.svg, file.svg
  and folder.svg;
- its menu mod (mods/menu): the base of files-enhanced/mods/files-enhanced/menu.js;
- its prompt and confirm mods (mods/prompt, mods/confirm): the base of
  files-enhanced/mods/files-enhanced/dialog.js;
- the Changes mod that ships with it (mods/changes; its source is herdrdev/herdr-app,
  defaults/mods/changes): the base of git-enhanced/mods/git-enhanced/ (main.js;
  the pages in changes.js and historypage.js, where.js, diffpane.js, filelist.js,
  commitbar.js, the read flags in scripts.js) and its icon changes.svg;
- the interface icons of its workspace-chrome mod, copied into
  files-enhanced/mods/files-enhanced/glyphs/ (among them check.svg, git-branch.svg, plus.svg,
  square-pen.svg) and git-enhanced/mods/git-enhanced/ (check.svg,
  git-branch.svg, plus.svg):
  Lucide icons, ISC, as the Herdr app's THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES says; glyphs/spinner.svg is
  Herdr's own;
- from the Herdr app 0.1.15, its tab bar, the tabs mod (mods/tabs): the base of
  herdr-enhanced/mods/tabs-enhanced/ (main.js; its icons win-close.svg, win-max.svg,
  win-min.svg and win-restore.svg unchanged);
- from the Herdr app 0.1.15, its worktree mod (mods/worktree): which space is in a worktree
  (place, spaceOf), the base of spaceFor in git-enhanced/mods/git-enhanced/worktrees.js;
- from the Herdr app 0.1.15, its main layout (layouts/main.json): the base of
  herdr-enhanced/layouts/herdr-enhanced.json, every node and field Herdr's but the tab bar's
  mod, the panel's pages and the preview's path;
- the six theme palettes it ships (graphite, ink, moss, paper, atom-one-dark, win98), as its
  theme() gives them, unchanged: the test data test/shared/themes.json.

Each of those files but the palettes, the unchanged icons and the layout says at its top that it is
based on Herdr's and changed; the layout's JSON can't, so herdr-enhanced/RECIPE.md says it. Other
code adapted from other projects (VS Code, Material Icon Theme, lazygit, Cline) and the Lucide icons
are listed with their licenses in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
